#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:2
msgid "Transactional updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:4
msgid ""
"A transactional update is an install or refresh operation on a set of snaps "
"that either succeeds for all the snaps, or, if even one snap encounters an "
"error, fails for all the entire set. If the process fails, all affected "
"snaps revert to their state before the process started, even snaps that "
"successfully updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:6
msgid ""
"This can help when a set of snaps with specific revisions are tested to "
"ensure they work together, and where behaviour could become unpredictable if "
"a set isn't installed or updated at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:8
msgid ""
"Transactional updates can also help when you know that one snap is dependent "
"on a specific revision of another, or when you need multiple snaps to update "
"at the same time. On the firmware for device running Ubuntu Core, for "
"example, it can help to update both the kernel snap and the gadget snap at "
"the same time. Transactional updates enable this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:10
msgid ""
"A transactional update or installation can be instantiated from either the "
"**snap** command, or from the {ref}`SnapD REST API <reference-development-"
"snapd-rest-api>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:12
msgid "Transactional updates from the snap command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:14
msgid ""
"The **snap install** and **snap refresh** commands accept an additional `--"
"transaction=` argument with either `all-snaps` to instantiate the process as "
"a single transaction, or `per-snap`, which is the default, for a separate "
"transaction per listed snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:16
msgid ""
"To install hello and hello-world snaps as a single transaction, for example, "
"run the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:18
msgid ""
"$ snap install hello hello-world --transaction=all-snaps\n"
"hello-world 6.4 from Canonical✓ installed\n"
"hello 2.10 from Canonical✓ installed\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/transactional-updates.md:24
msgid ""
"Currently, no change, log, or message is output to show if a set of snaps "
"have been installed as a single transaction."
msgstr ""
